# dconf profile for the initial-setup (wizard) session. GDM starts that
# session with DCONF_PROFILE=gnome-initial-setup, but the stock profile
# only exists in the system base (core26-desktop); a strictly confined
# session snap runs against its own base (core26), so without this copy
# the dconf client opens the null configuration and every GSettings read
# is empty (the wizard's layout selection then never reaches gnome-shell).
# Stock Ubuntu's profile also lists
# file-db:/usr/share/gnome-initial-setup/initial-setup-dconf-defaults;
# that file is not shipped in this image, so it is deliberately omitted
# rather than making dconf warn on every session start.
user-db:user
